    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 3,
        "sourceEnd": 52,
        "text": "Hi, Lisa. You look busy. What are you working on?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "2797e02e1c2924b58cb4af71ae9d22591a9ad4d31c6f08f76a7e0ae7941c5511",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 56,
        "sourceEnd": 189,
        "text": "Oh, hi, Tom. I’m preparing for a presentation about the recycling program at our university. It’s for my environmental science class.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "f0996463db961443fa73ab18140217cdfc04ea002aec5da08a2ba206b0304ff9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 193,
        "sourceEnd": 262,
        "text": "That’s interesting. I heard the program was started last year, right?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "e1ee794b7eea546a1ad2b78801f69052ff050804059c8bd3b5fe49aedc305200",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 266,
        "sourceEnd": 414,
        "text": "Yes, it was launched in September. At first, it wasn’t very successful. Many students didn’t know where the bins were, and the bins were often full.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "4055d43c070bb8af299c343a68d8f39193d5a9e06226bd8d372d66deea2bc2c9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 418,
        "sourceEnd": 434,
        "text": "So what changed?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "ca107b9da6d0fe2a39838f93f762e1609147297b5ba0699268d529172d161479",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 438,
        "sourceEnd": 593,
        "text": "Well, the university made some improvements. They added more bins and emptied them more often. Also, they trained student volunteers called “green guides.”",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "de82f3556a2ccaebe82d3a4f3b128d39cbed8eeede122c6f1ec884e51a2320c6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 597,
        "sourceEnd": 627,
        "text": "Green guides? What do they do?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "93ee5cbec226232d68fd42cfe24c17899fcf4d3bcb3448bfb6a6acaf35112890",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 631,
        "sourceEnd": 741,
        "text": "They stand near the bins during lunch and help people sort their waste. They answer questions and give advice.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "4da14f7980ab9c74bec4eb86359265bd7b08b7520c1a1b4731679f503223050b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 745,
        "sourceEnd": 795,
        "text": "That sounds helpful. Did the recycling rate go up?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "a2a6d3ad0558a40cefe1b36e9599408639515af30407e184a1dbf24f2c24e187",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 799,
        "sourceEnd": 905,
        "text": "Yes, it increased by 30% in three months. Now the university wants to expand the program to all buildings.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "205632845147c8b4cfc0999a402a3513d9d49041526133efd8eeaa3931eb97b6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 909,
        "sourceEnd": 1039,
        "text": "Great. By the way, I’m reading a long article for my history class. I find it hard to find specific information quickly. Any tips?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "b26a19ccfd658c833da42c80ff63d9fa62c24ef9fb95025bb388771de028eb58",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1043,
        "sourceEnd": 1213,
        "text": "Sure. First, look at the headings and subheadings. They show you the structure. Then, read the first and last sentences of each paragraph—those are often topic sentences.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "6fe2623715e75dcc9dbdbe3cf6ae1b4ebe61cbf2121886fe8dfbbd02d46a93cd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1217,
        "sourceEnd": 1248,
        "text": "Topic sentences? What are they?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "10ffe9bb961762d254adfeb4fc3b00b189570d38cee014e4dfa624138aaf699a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1252,
        "sourceEnd": 1359,
        "text": "They are sentences that give the main idea of the paragraph. Usually, they are at the beginning or the end.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "0256386742dc0ccd8cc892cafc429e9f484884d48a69be546cb800d0440d18cf",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1363,
        "sourceEnd": 1422,
        "text": "OK. And if I need a specific fact, like a date or a number?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "8e707a6c67a3488f4f96405725fb48eab3ff5da651224c72f1137500eedc6c29",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1426,
        "sourceEnd": 1532,
        "text": "Then you can scan. Scanning means looking quickly for numbers, names, or dates without reading every word.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "88590daed78ba24c188f8600bfab46f4baf911103e3040d42e5c85e9f77ba277",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1536,
        "sourceEnd": 1596,
        "text": "That’s useful. What about words like “however” or “because”?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "15073faf113ced681fa462b9c88e939806eae07f4872a42a49d4c56890aebb6a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1600,
        "sourceEnd": 1719,
        "text": "Those are signal words. They show relationships between ideas—like contrast or cause and effect. Pay attention to them.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "c38fbe7bb636d579c657b2ed64def70fab2833a03e504f503272a28e5f721711",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "m",
        "speaker": "M",
        "sourceStart": 1723,
        "sourceEnd": 1763,
        "text": "Thanks, Lisa. I’ll try these strategies.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "f489edc56875939fbf25bf857490af567d3339a11c6aa806bd45ec5c8f532695",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "w",
        "speaker": "W",
        "sourceStart": 1767,
        "sourceEnd": 1811,
        "text": "You’re welcome. Good luck with your reading!",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "ad0d84cd1d94b1554cc0290b5c0d572b66efaae90cb726fdc96f85e458855ba2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
